      "writtenOn": "2016-11-18T18:01:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah that is a workaround. \n\nNormally to connect a peripheral you need to define them like the UART is defined. It is like the second half of defining a gpio but peripherals use the FUNC macro instead of GPIO.\n\nPINMUX(FUNC(peripheral_name), pin, dio_flags)\n\nMost peripherals aren\u0027t directly connected to external pads, but some are like spi0 and sps0. That means those pads are being driven by default. The documentation has a document describing all peripherals that are directly connected and what pads they are connected to.\n\nThe SPI gpio declaration is a special case where we needed to override the default output behavior so that the pads would be tri-stated instead of driven by the peripheral. The only way to do that was to explicitly connect them to a gpio.",
